// Debug/observability with console(): printf-style messages to the host (JS),
// delivered over the event ring and formatted there. Numeric args (%d %u %x %c)
// are captured by value; %s copies up to 32 bytes from a packet pointer. The JS
// side handles them in a callback — log them, count them, ship them to a metrics
// pipe. Unlike log(), which snapshots payload bytes with a verdict, console() is
// a free-standing trace you can sprinkle anywhere in a program.
//
// Here: trace every HTTP request's port and first bytes, and flag big ones —
// without changing any verdict (the packets still pass).
filter {
  if (proto != 6) return pass;
  if (dport != 80) return pass;
  if (len == 0) return pass;                       // skip pure ACKs
  console("http :%d (%d bytes): %s", dport, len, payload);
  if (len > 1400) console("large request: %d bytes", len);
  return pass;
}
